  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1833b97b4e8284e489c3555d5dace838, type: 3}
  m_Name: SQL_07_DELETE
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.QuestionData
  id: SQL_07_DELETE
  language: 3
  topic: DELETE
  difficulty: 0
  questionType: 4
  questionText: The Note (id 2) turned out to be a shopping list. Which query removes
    only that row?
  code: 'Table: clues

    +----+----------+--------+

    | id | item     | room  
    |

    +----+----------+--------+

    |  1 | Backpack | Hall   |

    |  2 |
    Note     | Office |

    |  3 | Map      | Hall   |

    +----+----------+--------+'
  answerFormat: 0
  choices:
  - DELETE FROM clues WHERE id = 2;
  - DELETE FROM clues;
  - DELETE id = 2 FROM clues;
  - REMOVE FROM clues WHERE id = 2;
  correctChoiceIndex: 0
  monospaceChoices: 1
  acceptedAnswers: []
  caseSensitive: 1
  explanation: DELETE FROM table WHERE condition; removes only the matching rows.
    Without WHERE, DELETE FROM clues; would erase every clue! SQL has no REMOVE command.
  hint: Always pair DELETE with a WHERE clause.
